Subject: Cantor Inspection Runtime Seed P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 47cdb42d-6afe-404f-ba5d-81db1421310b
@ [specification_uuid] e3e7a424-c013-492a-a913-044ea17dc66d
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 6ea51dc3-5fb2-4a0c-b378-3615ac285430

& [ProblemAndChosenSeam]
  + consumer and official MCP are now implemented published and measured but client owners lack a small actual runtime/SOP artifact handoff
  + separately signed tooling can turn those exact binaries and real semantic seed into bounded portable bytes without app installation model hosting or new Rust semantic code
  + seven entries omit expected-response baggage and keep product generator/verifier execution-free; separate two-process development replay supplies actual cross-transport correspondence
  + real method/flags/local-central-end framing CRC32 and SHA256 checks are needed because equal compressed/uncompressed lengths alone are not a compression-method proof
  + create-new fresh scoped D leaves no replacement or deletion protect existing work and avoid another bulky target or tracked cache/binary growth
  + same-input archive reproducibility exact source/binary/seed identity and developer observations are useful but deliberately weaker than publisher authenticity trusted launch or full installation closure

& [DelineationAndPruning]
  + core Rust interface unchanged; only dev tooling fixtures guide and retained metadata are new
  + legacy four-binary bundle contributes read patterns not branch replacement cleanup execution or deployment authority
  + remove automatic extraction runtime invocation producer prebuilt override generic source-path selection expected-response archive and installation/service/provider/remote scope
  + final user-facing readiness remains an inspection component handoff not the full SOP-directed self-working Cantor agent

& [Caution]
  + physical path/reparse preflight is not a handle-bound hostile-NTFS security proof
  + target binaries can drift after all-feature workspace builds; rebuild the exact pinned production recipe before final package verification and require unchanged retained identity
  + CRC32 proves integrity only and SHA256 corresponds bytes; neither authenticates a publisher or model
